id: pm-beads-tjrz
title: Add beads diff for round-trip fidelity auditing
description: ""
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-06-09T17:55:38.612Z"
updated_at: "2026-06-09T21:43:27.040Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "pm beads diff <fileA> <fileB> and pm beads diff <file> --against-workspace classify per-bead added/removed/changed(fields)/unchanged keyed on bead id; --json structured output; --strict exits nonzero on drift, 0 otherwise; --filter-status/--filter-type reuse existing filter parsing; reuses export core + field mappers (no duplicated mapping logic); read-only; beads-diff rich-help alias; unit tests + README + changelog."
resolution: "Validated pm-beads diff against both exported file and live workspace using a complex fixture; status/type/priority normalization, dependencies, parent, labels, assignee/owner, and timestamp-preservation remained fidelity-safe."
expected_result: Complex Beads JSONL import->export and against-workspace diff should report no added/removed/changed beads.
actual_result: Release check passed and manual diff checks returned drift=false with unchanged=3 for both file-file and file-workspace comparisons.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-06-09T17:56:16.693Z",codex,"Design — `pm beads diff` (round-trip fidelity audit)\n\nKEY: match beads on the stable bead `id` (normalizeBeadKey: trim, case-preserving). Records without an id are skipped (cannot be matched across sources). First-occurrence wins on duplicate ids, mirroring buildBeadIndex. indexBeadsById(beads) builds the id→bead map per side.\n\nALGORITHM (diffBeads, pure, no I/O):\n- Optionally pre-filter BOTH sides via the existing RowFilter / beadPassesFilter (reused, not reimplemented).\n- For each id in A: if absent in B → removed; else compute changedFields(a,b) → if non-empty it is changed{id,fields}, else unchanged++.\n- For each id in B not in A → added.\n- Returns {added[], removed[], changed[{id,fields}], unchanged, countA, countB, drift}. Arrays sorted for stable output. drift = any added|removed|changed.\n\nFIELD COMPARISON SET (DIFF_FIELDS, exactly the round-trip-preserved fields): title, status, type, priority, tags, assignee, parent, deadline, dependencies. Comparison is SEMANTIC via normalizeDiffField, reusing the existing mappers so incidental formatting is not flagged as drift:\n- status → pmStatusToBeads(mapStatus(x)) so done==closed, wip==in_progress.\n- priority → mapPriority (so 2 == \"2\", clamped 0-4).\n- type → lowercased, default Task.\n- tags → trimmed, de-duped, SORTED (order-insensitive).\n- deadline → beadDeadline (honors deadline OR legacy due_date alias).\n- dependencies → set of upstream blocker ids via extractBlockerIds (collapses the many Beads edge spellings: dependencies[]/blocked_by string|array), SORTED, order-insensitive. So blocked_by:\"x\" == dependencies:[{id:x,kind:blocked_by}].\n\n--against-workspace: refactored runExport to extract buildBeadsFromWorkspace(pmRoot,{preserveIds,filter}) — the exact id-preservation + dependency translation + row-filter pipeline the on-disk exporter uses (readPmItems via spawnSync(\"pm\",[...,\"list-all\",\"--full\",\"--include-body\",\"--json\"]) → pmItemToBead). Diff parses the single file (parseBeadsFileForDiff, hard-fails on malformed JSON unlike the import parser) and diffs file(A) vs workspace(B). Exactly one file allowed in this mode. No SDK runtime import (import type only); workspace read stays on the existing spawnSync pattern. Strictly read-only — no mutations to workspace or files.\n\nOUTPUT: human summary to stderr by default (stdout stays clean for piping): A/B counts, per-class id lists, changed lines name the differing fields (e.g. \"~ bd-007 (status, tags)\"), unchanged count. Under --json the structured {a,b,added,removed,changed,unchanged,countA,countB,drift} object is returned (runtime serializes it). EXIT: exit 0 always UNLESS --strict AND drift → throws CommandError(GENERIC_FAILURE) in human mode / sets process.exitCode in --json mode (so the structured report still reaches the caller, matching the validate command's pattern). --filter-status/--filter-type reuse parseRowFilter.\n\nREGISTRATION: shared makeDiffCommand registered under canonical \"beads diff\" AND hyphenated \"beads-diff\" alias (mirrors makeValidateCommand). DIFF_FLAGS for rich help. No manifest change — `commands` capability already declared; verified manifest.json untouched.\n\nTESTS (14 new, all green, 48/48 total): identical lists→zero drift; semantic equality (done/closed, tag order, 2 vs \"2\"); added/removed detection; per-field change detection across all 8 scalar fields; dependency-edge change detection + edge-spelling equivalence; DIFF_FIELDS/normalizeDiffField/changedFields coverage incl due_date alias; row-filter scoping both sides; parseDiffOptions (options + global --json); command+alias registration; --against-workspace END-TO-END against a real fixture pm workspace (pm init → pm create with bead_id marker → buildBeadsFromWorkspace → spawnSync(\"pm\") → diff: file-only bead classified removed, matching bead unchanged); USAGE error without 2nd file / without --against-workspace; --strict throws on drift, returns cleanly when identical; malformed-JSONL hard-fail.\n\nVERIFY: release:check (typecheck, build, 48 tests pass, audit:prod, pack:dry-run, changelog:check) — see release:check run."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-06-09T21:42:39.745Z",codex-5-3,"Phase 5 verification: run complex Beads JSONL round-trip + beads diff fidelity checks against workspace export."
